  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-Vietnam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall goal of the project is to contribute to a sustainable socially just energy transition in Vietnam. The specific objective is to increase public and private-sector awareness of renewable energy (RE) and energy efficiency (EE) policies/programmes, and toensure that the effectiveness of RE/EE practices and initiatives are significantly raised, contributing to sustainable energy supply, consumption and security in Vietnam, the country&#x2019;s transition towards a low-carbon economy and increased gendersensitivity in theenergy sector.
The project has four key priorities: i) to equip key public and private stakeholders with understanding and knowledge of RE/EE policies, the effectiveness of RE/EE measures and initiatives; ii) to improve media communication and coverage on RE/EE and gender sensitivity in the energy sector; iii) to increase gender sensitive RE/EE practices in the daily life and businesses; iv) to increase the number of businesses accessing to investment for RE/EE practices. Gender sensitivity is integrated throughout the Action, ensuring that it not only contributes to Vietnam&#x2019;s sustainable energy targets but also ensures a gender equitable and sociallyjust energy transition.
The project was developed and implemented by a coalition of3partners Oxfam, VCCI, and the Vietnam Journalism Association. In this project, Oxfam will be responsible for overall management, coordination and strategy. Oxfam will provide technical support on policy recommendations, narratives, messages, campaigning,and engagement with the business sector and other stakeholders. Oxfam will comply with Vietnamese law and regulations on registration of projects and reporting to relevant authorities, ensuring that government counterparts are aware of project activitiesand outcomes. In addition, Oxfam will play the leading and coordinator role for activities around organizing and facilitating multi-stakeholder dialogues. Oxfam will use gender analysis and gender mainstreaming techniques, and a Gender at Work framework as an analytical tool. Oxfam in Vietnam will also  use Gender Action LearningSystem - Practical Guide for Transforming Gender and Unequal Power Relations based on community led empowerment methodology (GALS).Oxfam will mobilise its network of Global campaigning and public engagement. Oxfam International SME support and Private Sector Engagement Global Advisors will bring in broader international experience. Oxfam will identify opportunities for policy influencing anddraw on existing relationships with national government officials etc.</narrative>
  </description>
